# ios.rules
version: 1

## MUST
- No force-unwraps (`!`) on values that can realistically be nil from external input (network, user input, optional bindings); use `guard`/`if let` instead.
- No secrets, API keys, or signing credentials committed to the repo or Info.plist.
- All network responses are decoded through explicit `Codable` types, not manually parsed dictionaries.

## SHOULD
- New view controllers/views are covered by at least one unit or snapshot test.
- Long-running work is dispatched off the main thread with results delivered back on main.

## SECURITY
- Sensitive data (tokens, PII) is stored in the Keychain, not UserDefaults or plain files.
- App Transport Security exceptions (`NSAllowsArbitraryLoads`) are not introduced without a one-line justification.

## ARCHITECTURE
- View controllers/views do not perform networking directly; they go through a view model or service layer.
